@startuml a2_machine_locking
title A2 -- Community machine status state transitions

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam BackgroundColor white
skinparam state {
    BackgroundColor #fafafa
    BorderColor #555555
    FontSize 13
}

' ============================================================
' States
' ============================================================
state "available" as available
state "processing" as processing
state "idle" as idle

' ============================================================
' Existing transitions (black)
' ============================================================
[*] --> available : agent registers\n/ set_available

available --> idle : last_seen_at stale\n(auto, in get_available_community)
idle --> available : reconnect + heartbeat

' ============================================================
' NEW transitions added by A2 (green, bold)
' ============================================================
available -[#009900,bold]-> processing : claim_next_for_machine\n[NEW: SQL also writes\nmachines.status='processing']

processing -[#009900,bold]-> available : handle_chunk_succeeded\nhandle_chunk_failed\ncancel_render\n[NEW: lifecycle calls\nset_available on terminal]

processing -[#009900,bold]-> idle : last_seen_at stale\n[NEW: stale-sweep WHERE\nclause now covers\n'processing' too]

' ============================================================
' Notes
' ============================================================
note right of processing
  Allocator's get_available_community()
  filters status='available' only.
  Machines in 'processing' are excluded
  from new dispatches.
  Bug fixed: no more double-assignment.
end note

note left of available
  Before A2:
  Machine stays here for the entire
  duration of a job. Allocator returns
  it to a second concurrent render
  -- same PC tries to run two jobs.
end note

note as ImplNote #fffbe6
  **Files touched (4 files, ~25 lines)**

  serverV2/repositories/job_repository.py
    claim_next_for_machine: add third SQL
    UPDATE machines SET status='processing'
    conditional on a job row being returned

  serverV2/repositories/machine_repository.py
    get_available_community + mark_stale:
    extend WHERE clause from
    status='available' to
    status IN ('available','processing')

  serverV2/orchestrator/lifecycle.py
    constructor accepts machine_repo
    handle_chunk_succeeded / _failed / cancel_render:
    if machine_type=='windows' and machine_id:
        machine_repo.set_available(machine_id)

  serverV2/bootstrap.py
    pass machine_repo into RenderLifecycle()
end note

@enduml
